      "problem": "If $0.07c=2.8$, then $c=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $100$ to get rid of the decimals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.07c & =2.8 \\\\ 100\\cdot (0.07c) & =100\\cdot (2.8) \\\\ 7c & =280\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the above equation using the multiplication principle, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7c & =280 \\\\ \\frac{7c}{7} & =\\frac{280}{7} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{7}c}{\\cancel{7}} & =\\frac{280}{7} \\\\ c & =40\\end{aligned}\n$$",
